{"id":"sabirabad","qid":"Q2148635","category":"city","type":"oikonym","names":{"az":"Sabirabad","ru":"Сабирабад","en":"Sabirabad"},"coordinates":[48.47194,40.00528],"coordinatesSource":"wd","region":"mil-mugan","regionSource":"wp-az-regions","admin":[{"qid":"Q382132","az":"Sabirabad rayonu","en":"Sabirabad District"}],"firstRecord":{"year":1888,"precision":"year","bce":false,"kind":"inception","source":"wd"},"period":"modern","forms":[{"form":"Qalaqayın","lang":"az","from":1300,"to":1921,"sources":["wd"]},{"form":"Petropavlovka","lang":"az","to":1931,"sources":["wd"]},{"form":"Петропавловка","lang":"ru","to":1932,"sources":["wp-ru"]},{"form":"Петропавловка","lang":"ru","from":1887,"current":true,"sources":["wd"]},{"form":"Sabirabad","lang":"az","from":1931,"current":true,"sources":["wd"]}],"namedAfter":[],"etymology":[],"summary":{"az":{"text":"Sabirabad — Azərbaycan Respublikasının Sabirabad rayonunun Sabirabad şəhər inzibati ərazi dairəsində şəhər, Sabirabad rayonunun inzibati mərkəzi.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-az"},"ru":{"text":"Сабира́бад (азерб. Sabirabad) — город и административный центр Сабирабадского района Азербайджана.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-ru"},"en":{"text":"Sabirabad (also, Galagayin, Petropavlovka, and Petropavlovskoye) is the capital city of the Sabirabad District of Azerbaijan. The city was renamed in honor of the poet Mirza Alakbar Sabir. Sabirabad is the administrative center of Sabirabad District of the Republic of Azerbaijan. In 1935, the district received the status of subordinate city. Sabirabad is located on the right bank of the Kura River. In the vicinity of the city of Sugovushan, the Araz River is merged with the Kur River.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-en"}},"images":[{"thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Sabirabad_%C5%9F%C9%99h%C9%99ri.png/960px-Sabirabad_%C5%9F%C9%99h%C9%99ri.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","small":"https://thumb.wikimedia.o